<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<component type="desktop-application">
  <id>tech.redfoxlabs.Thirties</id>
  <metadata_license>CC0-1.0</metadata_license>
  <project_license>GPL-3.0-or-later</project_license>

  <name>Thirties</name>
  <summary>Plan your day with an assistant</summary>
  <description>
    <p>
      Thirties is a personal assistant for your time. It gathers your tasks and calendar into one place, lays the day out as 48 half-hour “thirties” anchored to sunrise and sunset, and lets you plan, re-plan and review the day in plain conversation, on your desktop or from your phone.
    </p>
    <p>Features include:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>A day canvas of thirties, with daylight and dark from your location</li>
      <li>Planning by conversation: “put the walk at 4:00”, “it went until 4:30”</li>
      <li>Your Joplin lists and GNOME calendars in one plan; it can tick off and add Joplin items for you</li>
      <li>Reminders and check-ins, on the desktop and by Telegram</li>
      <li>Rolling unfinished items into the next day, and learning how long things really take</li>
      <li>An assistant that runs on your computer (Gemma), or Gemini</li>
      <li>Sync between computers through a folder you choose</li>
    </ul>
    <p>This is an early alpha.</p>
  </description>

  <developer id="tech.redfoxlabs">
    <name>Matthew Samson (Red Fox Labs)</name>
  </developer>

  <url type="homepage">https://github.com/snakeeyes021/thirties</url>
  <url type="vcs-browser">https://github.com/snakeeyes021/thirties</url>
  <url type="bugtracker">https://github.com/snakeeyes021/thirties/issues</url>

  <translation type="gettext">thirties</translation>
  <launchable type="desktop-id">tech.redfoxlabs.Thirties.desktop</launchable>
  <content_rating type="oars-1.1" />

  <branding>
    <color type="primary" scheme_preference="light">#e9d4bb</color>
    <color type="primary" scheme_preference="dark">#7a5434</color>
  </branding>

  <releases>
    <release version="0.3.0" date="2026-11-11" type="development">
      <description>
        <p>In progress.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Nothing very sensitive goes to Gemini: passwords, PINs, keys and codes, card and bank numbers, ID numbers, and medication or diagnosis names are swapped for placeholders before a message leaves the computer, and put back in the reply</li>
          <li>Private notes (tagged "private" in Joplin, or in a list named Medical, Health or Finance) go to Gemini as item titles only, never their contents</li>
          <li>Safer Joplin writes: a change never overwrites an edit you make in the note at the same moment, a change Joplin saved without answering is never applied twice, and a morning's tidy-up of Today that has to wait never runs on a later day</li>
          <li>Items keep who they are when you reword, reorder or move them in Joplin: their plans, Today links and history follow them; a finished copy of a repeated item no longer hides the next copy, and an item written again after it was done is a new item</li>
          <li>Anything you add for today gets a time on the plan at once, in the first free time that fits; only when you say so ("if there's time", "no rush", "don't schedule it") does it go without one, under a new If there's time section at the end of the Agenda, the schedule message and the Today note</li>
          <li>If there's time items can be done, scheduled in the next gap, or put off to tomorrow, later this week, or dropped; a full day puts new things there and says so; when a free gap opens, a notice already being sent may name one of them; and what's left at the day's end comes back the next morning for this week</li>
          <li>Gemma on smaller devices: under 8 GB of memory, or after the bigger model fails to fit, Preferences offers the smaller model (Gemma 4 E2B); it's downloaded, checked and tested before the bigger one is removed, and Thirties never switches by itself</li>
          <li>Model downloads come from a fixed release of each file, so a new download is exactly the build that was tested</li>
          <li>Windows and order you state for today's items ("before the 4:00 call", "only between 10 and 3") are kept wherever an item is placed, even before it's planned; a time picked for you moves to the nearest one that keeps them, and a time you name that would break one is asked about once</li>
          <li>Nothing is removed or rearranged in your lists, memory or calendars unless you ask outright: archiving an item, rewording, splitting or moving list lines, forgetting something the assistant remembers, rewriting a profile section, or changing a whole calendar. Otherwise Thirties does the gentle version (a drop, an added line, hiding just that event) and says so, or asks first</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.2.1" date="2026-11-11" type="development">
      <description>
        <p>Dropping an item no longer changes your lists:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>A drop only stops an item rolling over: it stays on its list in Joplin, unticked, and can be planned again; the Archive in Before today keeps the record</li>
          <li>An item is taken off its list only when you ask for that outright ("archive it", "delete it")</li>
          <li>Items dropped earlier, when a drop still took them off their lists, are offered back once in Before today</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.2.0" date="2026-11-08" type="development">
      <description>
        <p>Mornings that start when you do, and a day that simply is the plan:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>One morning message, written fresh each day, at your wake-up time or at sunrise, optionally with the day's items; nothing else is sent until you reply</li>
          <li>Your reply is the morning: the day is built then, as the plan, with no approval step; the one question left is what doesn't fit today</li>
          <li>The morning routine goes on from when you're actually up, a part per half hour, alongside work, in a block it fits</li>
          <li>What's left from before takes effect by itself: today's items go on today's schedule, the rest wait for a day they fit, and proposed drops are applied after the day unless you say otherwise</li>
          <li>Agenda: a Before today tab beside Today (keep, drop, done, and an archive you can undrop from); the Free row and each routine show their time in the time column</li>
          <li>Dropped items are ticked and filed in Joplin in a monthly Dropped note beside the Done notes; undropping puts them back where they were</li>
          <li>Items show a short title everywhere; a long line's details stay out of messages and expand in the Agenda</li>
          <li>Check-ins come at their own time, or not at all</li>
          <li>Other people's calendar events stay out of the schedule sent in chat and Telegram</li>
          <li>Telegram lists are one item per line, without bullets</li>
          <li>A Joplin change that can't go through is set aside after a few tries, instead of being retried forever</li>
          <li>The assistant no longer says it can't make changes</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.1.0" date="2026-10-30" type="development">
      <description>
        <p>The day list, and an assistant you can trust with your lists:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Each Joplin note has a role (routine, today, list, project, reference) and each item an urgency</li>
          <li>A Today note: the day's list, linked to the lists its items came from</li>
          <li>The plan and the record kept apart: replan on request, nothing assumed done</li>
          <li>How often Thirties messages you: off, light, medium or high</li>
          <li>A Day page (now, next, not reported, done today) beside the timeline</li>
          <li>Items keep their real times; the day is shown in half-hour blocks; fixed things never move</li>
          <li>Only the exact item is ever changed in Joplin, and what's done is never offered again</li>
          <li>"Remind me to…" puts the thing on your plan, with a ping when it's time</li>
          <li>Telegram replies are retried, and start-of-block notices are kept in the chat</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.0.1" date="2026-10-17" type="development">
      <description>
        <p>First alpha of Thirties:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Setup assistant: location, usual week, assistant, Joplin, sync and phone</li>
          <li>Day planning by conversation, told in thirties</li>
          <li>Joplin lists and GNOME calendars, with write-back to Joplin</li>
          <li>Reminders, check-ins and start messages, on the desktop and by Telegram</li>
          <li>Morning rollover of unfinished items, and statistics from what actually happened</li>
          <li>Runs in the background, with autostart</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
  </releases>

</component>
